        "id": 202317,
        "name": "robertmaxfreeman",
        "username": "robertmaxfreeman",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/robertmaxfreeman/{size}/2147_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-08-13T15:07:57.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Nightmist, Absolute Zero, and Benchmark.  <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/grin.png?v=9\" title=\":grin:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":grin:\"></p>\n<p>Nightmist is the most underrated character in the game, in my opinion. You just can't be afraid of doing yourself damage. Cards will get you the relics and spells to control any situation, and heal yourself to boot!</p>\n<p>Termi-nation AZ has a lot of combo-opportunity in the right team, but for consistency, I like Freedom Five the best. </p>\n<p>Benchmark (especially his 'and Demand' variant) is a very powerful character than can be nearly unstoppable when properly equipped. I've got him to the point where every turn he was using fly-by to do 2 damage to 3 targets (it then went back to his hand), allowed another player to use a power, and then healed himself for 3-5 every turn. </p>",
        "post_number": 71,
        "post_type": 1,
